course: dictionary
lesson: 15585
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. You can tell which meaning is meant by reading the words around it. A symphony is a long piece of music for a full orchestra. «The symphony lasted almost forty minutes.» The clue is lasted for forty minutes, so symphony means a piece of music.
explain: A symphony can also be the orchestra itself. «The symphony walked on stage and tuned their instruments.» Musicians walk on stage and tune instruments, so here symphony means the group of players.
explain: A symphony of something is a rich mixture of things that go well together. «The garden was a symphony of colours.» Nobody is playing music here. The word means many colours blending beautifully, the way instruments blend in a piece of music.
fact: A symphony is usually in three or four parts called movements.
fact: «Symphony» means a long piece of music for a full orchestra.
fact: «A symphony of sounds» means many sounds blending together nicely.
fact: Beethoven's Fifth Symphony begins with a famous «da-da-da-DUM» rhythm.
fact: In the US, «the symphony» can mean the orchestra itself.
exercise: «The symphony lasted almost forty minutes.» What does symphony mean here? | A sudden loud bang | A fancy kind of cake | A small room for reading | *A long piece of music for a full orchestra
exercise: «The rain made a symphony of sounds on the roof.» What does symphony suggest? | *Many sounds blending together beautifully | A loud argument | One single quiet drip | A map of the town
exercise: Mia says, «Let's go to the symphony tonight.» What is most likely meant? | A game played with a ball | A dinner in a restaurant | A school trip to a farm | *A concert by an orchestra
test: «The orchestra tuned up before the symphony began.» What does symphony mean in this sentence? | A sudden storm | *A long piece of music | A bakery | A walk in the park
test: «Her painting was a symphony of bright colours.» What does symphony mean here? | A paintbrush | *Many colours blending together beautifully | A tired orchestra | Music played for a king
exam: Lena says «symphony» always means a piece of music. Is she completely right? | Yes, it only ever means a piece of music | Yes, but only in the US | No, it means a kind of bird | *No, it can also mean an orchestra or a mix of things that go well together
